Neogrok is a web frontend for zoekt, the trigram-based code search
engine. It offers live search as you type, syntax-highlighted results
and built-in documentation of the zoekt query language. Its only
backend is the JSON API of zoekt-webserver (started with -rpc).

It can also replace an existing OpenGrok site: deployed at the same
address, it redirects OpenGrok URLs to their neogrok equivalents and
translates OpenGrok's Lucene queries into zoekt queries.
